%% style: futureswheel
%% Futures wheel: what follows if a four-day work week becomes standard.
# Four-day work week becomes standard

## Three-day weekends
- More short domestic trips
  - Friday travel peaks
- More time for family care

## Longer working days
- Fatigue late in the day
  - More workplace errors
- Harder school pickups

## Fewer commuting days
- Lower transport emissions
- Less weekday transit revenue
  - Transit fares rise

## Services still open five days
- Staggered team rotas
  - Fewer shared meeting days
- Hiring to cover the fifth day

## Easier hiring and retention
- Lower staff turnover
  - Training costs fall
- Pressure on five-day employers
